From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000184 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: retire consumed P32 generation from rollback guards

Once P32R consumes the exact parked generation, no later completion or
controller cleanup callback may match it again. Treat the consumed record as
stale so a duplicate observation cannot rewrite the terminal R branch to X.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not
submission-ready.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_a72_membership.c
@@ -125,4 +125,5 @@ mt6797_a72_p32_target_locked(unsigned int cpu)
 	return a72_owner.health == MT6797_A72_OWNER_AVAILABLE &&
 		transaction->valid && transaction->p32_valid &&
+		transaction->p32.state != MT6797_A72_P32_STATE_CONSUMED &&
 		transaction->p32.abi == MT6797_A72_P32_ROLLBACK_ABI &&
 		transaction->p32.target_cpu == cpu &&
--
